  "body": "What happens: issue #1794 lists four review-artifact folders. PR #1823 removes them. Merged PRs put the same kind of evidence under `docs/` again, and #1794's inventory did not list them all. `git ls-files` on the merge of PR #1823 with `origin/main` db091cb38 shows:\n\n- `docs/review/1744/` : two PNGs, no README (added 2026-11-14 by 26f9eae18)\n- `docs/reviews/1699/` : README and two PNGs (added 2026-11-14 by af106857f, merged with PR #1699)\n- `docs/reviews/1710/` : README and four PNGs (added 2026-11-14 by 4bfb4b5a5)\n- `docs/reviews/1724/` : README, a check script and six PNGs\n\nFound while reviewing PR #1823. The first three folders are review evidence. Nothing in the tree links to them. Issue #1794 states where PR screenshots belong: the PR body, with images on the author fork's images-only branch.\n\n`docs/reviews/1724/` was retained by the decision in `docs/decisions/1122-form-seam-holes.md`. That decision cited the other checked-in folders as its precedent. PR #1823 removes that precedent. This issue must keep `docs/reviews/1724/` or move it, and record the choice.\n\n`crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/edge_click_modifiers.rs:227` keeps the opt-in `BOUNDARY_REVIEW_IMAGES` capture hook. It creates its output directory. A refresh run against the product tree would recreate a folder the pin test rejects. Move the hook's default target to a scratch directory, or drop the hook.\n\nDone means: `docs/review/1744`, `docs/reviews/1699` and `docs/reviews/1710` are gone from `main`; `docs/reviews/1724` has a recorded keep-or-move decision; the xtask test `reviewed_screenshot_directories_are_absent` names every folder this issue removes; and `git grep` finds no reference to a removed path.\n",
